Falsifies `byte_glob::verification::a_prepared_pattern_agrees_with_the_plain_match`.

The defect: a prepared pattern checks only the tail after the last `*` and never matches the head, so
`a*b` prepared matches `xb`.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(Pattern::new(p).matches_with(n, options), matches_with(p, n, options))`.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -491,7 +491,8 @@ impl<'a> Pattern<'a> {
             };
         }
         // The head ends in that `*`, which absorbs whatever the rest of the head leaves over.
-        match_steps(&self.bytes[..tail_start], head_name, options).matched
+        let _ = head_name;
+        true
     }
 }
 
